# Prettier is only meant to format files under src/ (see package.json's
# own "format" script: `prettier --write "src/**/*"`). Ignoring
# everything else here, rather than relying solely on that glob, keeps
# behavior consistent regardless of how Prettier gets invoked —
# directly via that script, through an editor/IDE integration, or via
# lint-staged — since .prettierignore is always respected no matter
# what glob (if any) the caller passes in.
/*
!/src

# .vue files are excluded from Prettier entirely, everywhere under
# src/ — ESLint (via eslint-plugin-vue) owns formatting for them
# instead (see the "lint"/"lint:fix" scripts), since Prettier's own
# .vue support doesn't handle template-specific formatting the same,
# more Vue-aware way.
src/**/*.vue
